{
  "version": 1,
  "_doc": "Rover missions on the surface (src/rover/rover_missions.gd). A rover mission in operation (a 'rover' project, or any surface project whose payload carries a rover built in the workshop) offers 'Controlar o rover' on the solar-system map once it has arrived: the surface opens with that rover and the objectives of its briefing ('briefing:<id>'), else of its target ('target:<id>'). The player may also leave it in automatic: when the mission ends, every objective the rover can do by itself (it has the tool, the range, the climb, air for the drone, power for the night) is done at auto_science of its science. Objective fields: SurfaceSession (kind, poi_kind, label_key, science, offset [x, z] m from the landing site for the fallback marker, amount, need = rover tool) plus auto rules: climb (degrees the way there needs), night (the place needs RTG or a big battery to keep working). drive_science_cap: a mission's drives credit at most this x the sum of its objectives' science (no farming).",
